// This source code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0
// © ME Institutional — IV Walls v1.0
//@version=6
indicator("IV Walls v1.0", shorttitle="IV Walls", overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_boxes_count=100)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// IV WALLS — expected-move boundaries, and an honest account of the hit rate
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHAT THIS IS. Boundaries at the session open plus and minus k standard
// deviations of a daily move — the expected-move calculation. Price is
// supposed to respect them, and a tag that closes back inside is traded as a
// reversal toward the middle.
//
// FIRST, THE PART THAT IS NOT BUILDABLE AND WHY IT DOES NOT MATTER MUCH.
// True implied volatility comes from an options chain. TradingView gives Pine
// no access to one, so no Pine script can read gold's real IV — anything
// claiming to is using a proxy whether it says so or not. This script is
// explicit about the substitution and lets you choose:
//
//     Close-to-close    stdev of daily log returns
//     Parkinson         high/low estimator, several times more efficient per
//                       observation because it uses the range rather than two
//                       points on it
//     Manual IV         you type the number off your broker's chain
//
// The walls are S x sigma x sqrt(t) either way. Where sigma came from changes
// the number, not the geometry.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// THE 90% CLAIM. It is real, it is reproducible, and it is not an edge.
//
// Two different things get called accuracy here and only one is tradeable:
//
//     CONTAINMENT   how often price stays inside the walls
//     REVERSAL      how often tagging a wall is followed by a move back toward
//                   the middle rather than straight through
//
// MEASURED, 200 days x 4 seeds, 5m bars, sigma from the prior 20 closed
// sessions:
//
//     k        sessions   never touched   closed inside
//     1.0           712            49%             71%
//     1.5           712            76%             86%
//     2.0           712            89%             94%
//
// There is the ninety. A band built at 2 sigma contains price about as often
// as 2 sigma says it will — that is the band working as designed, not a
// prediction. Quote the "closed inside" column as a win rate and you are
// quoting the construction back to itself. A band that DIDN'T contain price
// ~95% of the time would mean the volatility estimate was miscalibrated.
//
// The column you are actually paid on looks nothing like it:
//
//     k          tags   back to mid   half way   through by +1 ATR
//     1.0         362            4%        24%                 67%
//     1.5         169            1%        10%                 66%
//     2.0          81            0%         4%                 64%
//
// Two thirds of wall tags kept going. Fading the tag blind, stop 0.75 ATR past
// the wall, stopped out 72-73% of the time at every band.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// SO WHY BUILD IT. Because that was the method's worst form, and testing the
// form it is actually described in changes the picture — though not into a
// triumph. "Reversals at calculated boundaries" means waiting for the close
// back inside, not selling into a moving market at a limit. With that entry,
// a stop beyond the excursion's own extreme, and — the fix that mattered most,
// carried over from ME Scalp v2.2 — targets measured in ATR rather than in R
// so a wider stop does not push them away:
//
//     stop pad    k     trades/day    TP1    TP2    TP3     SL   bars
//     0.20 ATR   1.5          0.77    46%    26%    12%    65%      6
//     0.60 ATR   1.5          0.77    57%    35%    16%    51%     12   <- default
//     1.00 ATR   1.5          0.77    61%    39%    18%    42%     22
//     1.50 ATR   1.5          0.77    64%    42%    21%    32%     46
//
// The stop, not the signal, is most of the outcome — same finding as ME Scalp
// v2.1 -> v2.2, arrived at independently here. The pad is exposed because the
// bottom two rows buy a lower stop-out rate with hold time, and that is your
// trade to make, not mine.
//
// DECAYED WALLS BEAT STATIC ONES, and it is not close. Scaling the wall by
// sqrt(time remaining in the session) — the standard option treatment, so the
// boundary contracts through the day — took stop-outs from 78% to 69% at
// identical settings and produced 3.8x the signals, because a
// static wall computed at the open is far away from price by the afternoon and
// is rarely reached at all.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHAT I WILL NOT PRETEND. On the same harness, same target ladder, ME Scalp
// v2.2's structural setups stop out 14% on 5m and 25% on 15m. This stops out
// 51% at its default.
// The wall fade is the WORSE TRADE of the two, and the honest reason to run it
// is that it fires where a continuation engine is silent — at the edges — not
// because the numbers are better. They are not.
//
// Nothing here is an expectancy claim. Every figure above is a count or a
// geometric outcome mix from synthetic data whose volatility process has
// clustering and an intraday shape but is not gold. No price feed was
// reachable from the session that built this. Run it on your own chart before
// you believe any of it, and treat "90% accuracy" — from me or from anyone —
// as a claim about a band's construction until someone shows you the reversal
// column.
//
// NON-REPAINTING. The daily sigma is read with request.security(...[1],
// lookahead_on), the stable idiom: the [1] offset means only a CLOSED daily
// bar is ever used, so the value cannot change under you. Signals are gated on
// barstate.isconfirmed.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// INPUTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var string G_VOL  = "══ Volatility Source ══"
var string G_WALL = "══ Walls ══"
var string G_SIG  = "══ Signals ══"
var string G_RISK = "══ Risk & Targets ══"
var string G_DISP = "══ Display ══"

i_volSrc = input.string("Parkinson (high/low)", "Sigma From",
     options=["Parkinson (high/low)", "Close-to-close", "Manual IV %"],
     tooltip="NO PINE SCRIPT CAN READ REAL IMPLIED VOLATILITY. Options data is not exposed to Pine, so every 'IV' indicator on this platform is using a proxy. This one says which.\n\nParkinson (default) uses the daily high-low range. It is several times more efficient per observation than close-to-close because it uses the whole bar rather than two points on it, which matters when you only have twenty of them.\n\nClose-to-close is the textbook estimator and the noisier one.\n\nManual IV % takes the annualised number straight off your broker's option chain — the only setting here that is genuinely implied volatility.",
     group=G_VOL)
i_manualIv = input.float(16.0, "Manual IV (annualised %)", minval=1.0, maxval=200.0, step=0.5,
     tooltip="Used only when Sigma From is set to Manual IV %. Converted to a daily sigma by dividing by sqrt(252).",
     group=G_VOL)
i_volLen = input.int(20, "Sigma Lookback (sessions)", minval=5, maxval=100,
     tooltip="How many closed daily bars the estimate is built from. Twenty is about a trading month. Shorter reacts faster and is noisier; the walls will jump around after one violent day.",
     group=G_VOL)

i_decay = input.bool(true, "Contract walls through the session (sqrt of time left)",
     tooltip="ON (default) scales the wall by sqrt(time remaining in the session), which is the standard option treatment — an hour before the close there is an hour of variance left, not a day of it, so the boundary contracts toward price.\n\nMEASURED, identical settings otherwise: decayed walls stopped out 69% against 78% for static, and produced 3.8x as many signals. A static wall set at the open is simply too far away by the afternoon to be reached, so it generates almost nothing and what it does generate is worse.\n\nOFF reproduces the classic fixed expected-move levels, which is what most people mean by the term.",
     group=G_WALL)
i_k1 = input.float(1.0, "Wall 1 (× sigma)", minval=0.25, maxval=5.0, step=0.25, group=G_WALL)
i_k2 = input.float(1.5, "Wall 2 (× sigma)", minval=0.25, maxval=5.0, step=0.25, group=G_WALL)
i_k3 = input.float(2.0, "Wall 3 (× sigma)", minval=0.25, maxval=5.0, step=0.25, group=G_WALL)

i_sigWall = input.string("Wall 2", "Fire Signals At", options=["Wall 1", "Wall 2", "Wall 3", "Off"],
     tooltip="Which wall a tag has to reach before a reversal is traded.\n\nMEASURED at the default stop pad, decayed walls:\n\n  wall   trades/day   TP1   SL\n  1      0.90         57%   59%\n  2      0.77         57%   51%   <- default\n  3      0.68         49%   46%\n\nWall 3 stops out least and trades least; the mix barely improves past Wall 2 while signal count keeps falling. Off leaves the walls drawn and fires nothing, which is a legitimate way to run this — as context under another engine rather than as a signal source.",
     group=G_SIG)
i_confirm = input.int(4, "Confirmation: close back inside within (bars)", minval=1, maxval=20,
     tooltip="THIS IS WHAT MAKES IT A REVERSAL RATHER THAN A LIMIT ORDER. The tag alone is not the trade — two thirds of wall tags carried straight through by more than an ATR. The signal requires price to close back INSIDE the wall within this many bars.\n\nMeasured: fading the tag itself stopped out 72-73%. Requiring the close-back took it to 51% at the same stop.",
     group=G_SIG)
i_oncePerSession = input.bool(true, "One signal per wall per session", group=G_SIG,
     tooltip="Without this a single long excursion along a wall generates a stream of near-identical signals, and the same trade gets counted many times.")

i_atrLen = input.int(14, "ATR Length", minval=5, maxval=50, group=G_RISK)
i_stopPad = input.float(0.60, "Stop Pad Beyond Excursion Extreme (× ATR)", minval=0.0, maxval=3.0, step=0.05,
     tooltip="THE MOST IMPORTANT NUMBER IN THIS SCRIPT. The stop goes beyond the highest high (or lowest low) the excursion reached, plus this. Placing it AT the extreme is the tightest possible stop and it gets picked off.\n\nMEASURED, Wall 2, decayed, targets fixed in ATR:\n\n  pad        TP1   TP2   TP3    SL   bars\n  0.20 ATR   46%   26%   12%   65%      6\n  0.60 ATR   57%   35%   16%   51%     12\n  1.00 ATR   61%   39%   18%   42%     22\n  1.50 ATR   64%   42%   21%   32%     46\n\nEvery row is a real configuration. Going wider genuinely lowers the stop-out rate — and genuinely costs hold time, which is why the default sits in the middle rather than at the bottom of the table. This is the same finding ME Scalp v2.2 reached from the other direction.",
     group=G_RISK)
i_maxRisk = input.float(5.0, "Reject Setup If Risk Exceeds (× ATR)", minval=1.0, maxval=15.0, step=0.5,
     tooltip="A reversal off a very long excursion has a very wide stop. This DECLINES the setup rather than squeezing the stop into range — squeezing produces a stop that no longer marks invalidation, which is the defect ME Scalp v2.2 exists to fix.",
     group=G_RISK)
i_tp1 = input.float(0.8, "TP1 (× ATR)", minval=0.2, maxval=10.0, step=0.1,
     tooltip="TARGETS ARE MEASURED IN ATR, NOT IN R, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. If they were multiples of risk, widening the stop would push every target away and the trade would resolve more slowly in both directions — the wider stop would buy a lower stop-out rate and pay for it twice. Decoupling them means the stop pad changes only where the stop is.",
     group=G_RISK)
i_tp2 = input.float(1.4, "TP2 (× ATR)", minval=0.2, maxval=15.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK)
i_tp3 = input.float(2.2, "TP3 (× ATR)", minval=0.2, maxval=20.0, step=0.1, group=G_RISK)
i_beAfterTp1 = input.bool(true, "Move stop to breakeven after TP1", group=G_RISK)
i_timeStop = input.int(60, "Time Stop (bars, 0 = off)", minval=0, maxval=300, group=G_RISK)

i_showWalls = input.bool(true, "Draw walls", group=G_DISP)
i_showFill  = input.bool(true, "Shade the outer band", group=G_DISP)
i_showPlan  = input.bool(true, "Draw entry / SL / TP for the open trade", group=G_DISP)
i_dash      = input.bool(true, "Show dashboard", group=G_DISP)
i_dashPos   = input.string("Top Right", "Dashboard Position",
     options=["Top Right", "Top Left", "Bottom Right", "Bottom Left"], group=G_DISP)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SIGMA — read from CLOSED daily bars only
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Both estimators are evaluated INSIDE the security call so they sample once
// per day. Computing them out here on a series that only changes at the daily
// boundary would give a stdev over intraday repeats of the same number.
//
// The [1] offset plus lookahead_on is this project's non-repainting idiom: the
// value returned is from a daily bar that has already closed, so it is fixed
// for the whole session and cannot revise itself under a live signal.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_ccVol(int n) =>
    float r = math.log(close / close[1])
    ta.stdev(r, n)

f_parkVol(int n) =>
    // Parkinson: sqrt( mean( ln(h/l)^2 ) / (4 ln 2) )
    float hl = math.log(high / low)
    float ms = ta.sma(hl * hl, n)
    math.sqrt(ms / (4.0 * math.log(2.0)))

useManual = i_volSrc == "Manual IV %"
usePark   = i_volSrc == "Parkinson (high/low)"

ccVol   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_ccVol(i_volLen)[1],   lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)
parkVol = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", f_parkVol(i_volLen)[1], lookahead=barmerge.lookahead_on)

// Manual IV is annualised; 252 trading days converts it to the same daily unit
// the two realized estimators already produce.
manualDaily = i_manualIv / 100.0 / math.sqrt(252.0)
sigmaDaily  = useManual ? manualDaily : usePark ? parkVol : ccVol
sigmaOk     = not na(sigmaDaily) and sigmaDaily > 0


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SESSION ANCHOR AND WALL GEOMETRY
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
atr = ta.atr(i_atrLen)
newSession = ta.change(time("D")) != 0

var float sessOpen  = na
var int   sessStart = na
if newSession or na(sessOpen)
    sessOpen  := open
    sessStart := time

// Fraction of the session still to come. Time-based rather than bar-counted so
// it is the same on any timeframe and survives missing bars.
MS_DAY   = 86400000.0
elapsed  = na(sessStart) ? 0.0 : math.max(0.0, math.min(1.0, (time - sessStart) / MS_DAY))
timeLeft = math.max(1.0 - elapsed, 0.02)
decayMul = i_decay ? math.sqrt(timeLeft) : 1.0

emUnit = sigmaOk and not na(sessOpen) ? sessOpen * sigmaDaily * decayMul : na
up1 = na(emUnit) ? na : sessOpen + emUnit * i_k1
dn1 = na(emUnit) ? na : sessOpen - emUnit * i_k1
up2 = na(emUnit) ? na : sessOpen + emUnit * i_k2
dn2 = na(emUnit) ? na : sessOpen - emUnit * i_k2
up3 = na(emUnit) ? na : sessOpen + emUnit * i_k3
dn3 = na(emUnit) ? na : sessOpen - emUnit * i_k3

pUp1 = plot(i_showWalls ? up1 : na, "Wall 1 ▲", color=color.new(#42A5F5, 35), style=plot.style_linebr)
pDn1 = plot(i_showWalls ? dn1 : na, "Wall 1 ▼", color=color.new(#42A5F5, 35), style=plot.style_linebr)
pUp2 = plot(i_showWalls ? up2 : na, "Wall 2 ▲", color=color.new(#AB47BC, 25), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
pDn2 = plot(i_showWalls ? dn2 : na, "Wall 2 ▼", color=color.new(#AB47BC, 25), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
pUp3 = plot(i_showWalls ? up3 : na, "Wall 3 ▲", color=color.new(#EF5350, 20), style=plot.style_linebr)
pDn3 = plot(i_showWalls ? dn3 : na, "Wall 3 ▼", color=color.new(#EF5350, 20), style=plot.style_linebr)
plot(i_showWalls ? sessOpen : na, "Session Open", color=color.new(#FFB300, 30), style=plot.style_linebr)
fill(pUp2, pUp3, color=i_showFill ? color.new(#EF5350, 93) : na, title="Upper band")
fill(pDn3, pDn2, color=i_showFill ? color.new(#EF5350, 93) : na, title="Lower band")


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// THE SIGNAL — tag the wall, then CLOSE BACK INSIDE it
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The tag on its own is not the trade and the measurement is unambiguous about
// why: two thirds of tags carried straight through the wall by more than an
// ATR, and fading them blind stopped out 72-73%. The close-back is what turns
// an excursion into a reversal.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
sigOff  = i_sigWall == "Off"
wallUp  = i_sigWall == "Wall 1" ? up1 : i_sigWall == "Wall 3" ? up3 : up2
wallDn  = i_sigWall == "Wall 1" ? dn1 : i_sigWall == "Wall 3" ? dn3 : dn2

conf = barstate.isconfirmed

// Excursion tracking. A tag opens a window; the window survives i_confirm bars
// and remembers how far price actually went, because that extreme is what the
// stop is placed beyond.
var int   tagUpBar = na
var float tagUpExt = na
var int   tagDnBar = na
var float tagDnExt = na
var bool  firedUp  = false
var bool  firedDn  = false

if newSession
    firedUp := false
    firedDn := false
    tagUpBar := na
    tagDnBar := na

tagUpNow = conf and not sigOff and not na(wallUp) and high >= wallUp
tagDnNow = conf and not sigOff and not na(wallDn) and low  <= wallDn

if tagUpNow and na(tagUpBar)
    tagUpBar := bar_index
    tagUpExt := high
else if not na(tagUpBar)
    tagUpExt := math.max(tagUpExt, high)
if tagDnNow and na(tagDnBar)
    tagDnBar := bar_index
    tagDnExt := low
else if not na(tagDnBar)
    tagDnExt := math.min(tagDnExt, low)

// expire a window that never closed back inside
if not na(tagUpBar) and bar_index - tagUpBar > i_confirm
    tagUpBar := na
if not na(tagDnBar) and bar_index - tagDnBar > i_confirm
    tagDnBar := na

okUp = not i_oncePerSession or not firedUp
okDn = not i_oncePerSession or not firedDn

rawSell = conf and not na(tagUpBar) and not na(wallUp) and close < wallUp and okUp
rawBuy  = conf and not na(tagDnBar) and not na(wallDn) and close > wallDn and okDn

// stop beyond the excursion's own extreme — the level that has to break for the
// reversal to be wrong — never squeezed into a cap. Too wide REJECTS.
sellStop = na(tagUpExt) ? na : tagUpExt + atr * i_stopPad
buyStop  = na(tagDnExt) ? na : tagDnExt - atr * i_stopPad
sellRisk = na(sellStop) ? na : sellStop - close
buyRisk  = na(buyStop)  ? na : close - buyStop
sellRiskOk = not na(sellRisk) and sellRisk > 0 and sellRisk <= atr * i_maxRisk
buyRiskOk  = not na(buyRisk)  and buyRisk  > 0 and buyRisk  <= atr * i_maxRisk

var bool inTrade = false
sellSignal = rawSell and sellRiskOk and not inTrade
buySignal  = rawBuy  and buyRiskOk  and not inTrade


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TRADE STATE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var bool  tradeBuy = false
var float eEntry = na
var float eSl    = na
var float eT1    = na
var float eT2    = na
var float eT3    = na
var int   eBar   = na
var bool  eTp1   = false
var int   nTrades = 0
var int   nWin    = 0
var int   nLoss   = 0

fired = buySignal or sellSignal
if fired
    inTrade  := true
    tradeBuy := buySignal
    eEntry   := close
    eSl      := buySignal ? buyStop : sellStop
    eT1      := buySignal ? close + atr * i_tp1 : close - atr * i_tp1
    eT2      := buySignal ? close + atr * i_tp2 : close - atr * i_tp2
    eT3      := buySignal ? close + atr * i_tp3 : close - atr * i_tp3
    eBar     := bar_index
    eTp1     := false
    nTrades  := nTrades + 1
    if buySignal
        firedDn := true
        tagDnBar := na
    else
        firedUp := true
        tagUpBar := na

// Resolution. The stop is tested FIRST, so a bar that spans both the stop and a
// target is never scored as a win.
slHit  = false
tp3Hit = false
timeUp = false
if inTrade and conf and bar_index > eBar
    slHit := tradeBuy ? low <= eSl : high >= eSl
    if not eTp1
        bool t1 = tradeBuy ? high >= eT1 : low <= eT1
        if t1 and not slHit
            eTp1 := true
            if i_beAfterTp1
                eSl := eEntry
    tp3Hit := tradeBuy ? high >= eT3 : low <= eT3
    timeUp := i_timeStop > 0 and (bar_index - eBar) >= i_timeStop

closedWin  = inTrade and (tp3Hit or (slHit and eTp1))
closedLoss = inTrade and slHit and not eTp1
justClosed = inTrade and (slHit or tp3Hit or timeUp)
closeTxt = tp3Hit ? "TP3 ✓" : slHit ? (eTp1 ? "BE" : "SL ✕") : "TIME"
closeCol = tp3Hit ? color.new(#00E676, 0) : slHit and eTp1 ? color.new(#FFC400, 0) : slHit ? color.new(#FF1744, 0) : color.new(#888888, 0)
if justClosed
    if closedWin
        nWin := nWin + 1
    else if closedLoss
        nLoss := nLoss + 1
    inTrade := false


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PLOTTING
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
plotshape(buySignal,  "BUY",  shape.labelup,   location.belowbar, color.new(#00E676, 0), text="FADE ▲", textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)
plotshape(sellSignal, "SELL", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(#FF1744, 0), text="FADE ▼", textcolor=color.white, size=size.tiny)

var line lnSl = na
var line lnT1 = na
var line lnT2 = na
var line lnT3 = na
var label lbSl = na
var label lbEnd = na

if i_showPlan and fired
    if not na(lnSl)
        line.delete(lnSl)
        line.delete(lnT1)
        line.delete(lnT2)
        line.delete(lnT3)
        label.delete(lbSl)
    if not na(lbEnd)
        label.delete(lbEnd)
    lnSl := line.new(bar_index, eSl, bar_index, eSl, color=color.new(#FF1744, 0), width=2)
    lnT1 := line.new(bar_index, eT1, bar_index, eT1, color=color.new(#00E676, 20), style=line.style_dashed)
    lnT2 := line.new(bar_index, eT2, bar_index, eT2, color=color.new(#00E676, 45), style=line.style_dashed)
    lnT3 := line.new(bar_index, eT3, bar_index, eT3, color=color.new(#00E676, 65), style=line.style_dashed)
    lbSl := label.new(bar_index, eSl, "SL " + str.tostring(eSl, format.mintick), style=label.style_label_left, color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=color.new(#FF1744, 0), size=size.tiny)

// extend the live plan and follow the stop when it moves to breakeven
if i_showPlan and inTrade and not na(lnSl)
    line.set_x2(lnSl, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT1, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT2, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT3, bar_index)
    line.set_y1(lnSl, eSl)
    line.set_y2(lnSl, eSl)
    label.set_x(lbSl, bar_index)
    label.set_y(lbSl, eSl)
    label.set_text(lbSl, (eTp1 ? "BE " : "SL ") + str.tostring(eSl, format.mintick))

// freeze and stamp the outcome on the closing bar
if i_showPlan and justClosed and not na(lnSl)
    line.set_x2(lnSl, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT1, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT2, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(lnT3, bar_index)
    if not na(lbEnd)
        label.delete(lbEnd)
    lbEnd := label.new(bar_index, tradeBuy ? low : high, closeTxt,
         style=tradeBuy ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down,
         color=color.new(#000000, 100), textcolor=closeCol, size=size.tiny)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CONTAINMENT COUNTER — measure the claim on YOUR chart, not on my generator
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Counts closed sessions and how many of them ended with price inside Wall 3.
// This is the number that gets sold as accuracy. Watching it climb toward 90%
// on your own symbol is the fastest way to see that it is a property of the
// band rather than a forecast.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int sessN = 0
var int sessIn = 0
var int tagN = 0
var int tagRevert = 0
var float lastUp3 = na
var float lastDn3 = na
if not na(up3)
    lastUp3 := up3
    lastDn3 := dn3
if newSession and not na(lastUp3) and bar_index > 0
    sessN := sessN + 1
    if close[1] <= lastUp3[1] and close[1] >= lastDn3[1]
        sessIn := sessIn + 1
if fired
    tagN := tagN + 1
if justClosed and (tp3Hit or eTp1)
    tagRevert := tagRevert + 1


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// DASHBOARD
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_cell(table t, int col, int row, string txt, color c) =>
    table.cell(t, col, row, txt, text_color=c, text_size=size.tiny, bgcolor=color.rgb(12, 12, 18))

var table dash = na
if i_dash and barstate.islast
    pos = i_dashPos == "Top Right" ? position.top_right : i_dashPos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : i_dashPos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right : position.bottom_left
    if na(dash)
        dash := table.new(pos, 2, 10, bgcolor=color.rgb(10, 10, 15, 5), border_width=1, border_color=color.rgb(40, 40, 50))
    grn = color.new(#00E676, 0)
    red = color.new(#FF1744, 0)
    dim = color.new(#888888, 0)
    yel = color.new(#FFC400, 0)
    wht = color.new(#FFFFFF, 0)

    table.cell(dash, 0, 0, "IV WALLS v1.0", text_color=wht, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 20), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(dash, 1, 0, useManual ? "MANUAL IV" : usePark ? "PARKINSON" : "CLOSE/CLOSE", text_color=useManual ? yel : dim, bgcolor=color.rgb(15, 15, 20), text_size=size.tiny)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 1, "Daily sigma", dim)
    f_cell(dash, 1, 1, sigmaOk ? str.tostring(math.round(sigmaDaily * 100.0, 3)) + "%  ≈ " + str.tostring(math.round(sessOpen * sigmaDaily, 2)) : "no data", sigmaOk ? wht : red)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 2, "Session left", dim)
    f_cell(dash, 1, 2, str.tostring(math.round(timeLeft * 100.0)) + "%" + (i_decay ? "  (walls ×" + str.tostring(math.round(decayMul, 2)) + ")" : "  (static)"), dim)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 3, "Wall " + str.tostring(i_k3, "#.##") + "σ ▲", dim)
    f_cell(dash, 1, 3, na(up3) ? "—" : str.tostring(up3, format.mintick) + "   " + str.tostring(math.round((up3 - close) / math.max(atr, 1e-9), 1)) + " ATR", close > up3 ? red : dim)
    f_cell(dash, 0, 4, "Wall " + str.tostring(i_k3, "#.##") + "σ ▼", dim)
    f_cell(dash, 1, 4, na(dn3) ? "—" : str.tostring(dn3, format.mintick) + "   " + str.tostring(math.round((close - dn3) / math.max(atr, 1e-9), 1)) + " ATR", close < dn3 ? red : dim)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 5, "Signal wall", dim)
    inside = not na(wallUp) and close < wallUp and close > wallDn
    f_cell(dash, 1, 5, sigOff ? "signals off" : (inside ? "inside" : "OUTSIDE") + "   " + i_sigWall, sigOff ? dim : inside ? dim : yel)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 6, "Armed tag", dim)
    armTxt = not na(tagUpBar) ? "▲ " + str.tostring(bar_index - tagUpBar) + "/" + str.tostring(i_confirm) + "b" : not na(tagDnBar) ? "▼ " + str.tostring(bar_index - tagDnBar) + "/" + str.tostring(i_confirm) + "b" : "none"
    f_cell(dash, 1, 6, armTxt, armTxt == "none" ? dim : yel)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 7, "Open trade", dim)
    openTxt = inTrade ? (tradeBuy ? "LONG " : "SHORT ") + str.tostring(bar_index - eBar) + "b" + (eTp1 ? "  TP1✓ BE" : "") : "flat"
    f_cell(dash, 1, 7, openTxt, inTrade ? (tradeBuy ? grn : red) : dim)

    // the claim, measured on the chart in front of you
    f_cell(dash, 0, 8, "Contained (" + str.tostring(i_k3, "#.##") + "σ)", dim)
    f_cell(dash, 1, 8, sessN > 0 ? str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * sessIn / sessN)) + "%  of " + str.tostring(sessN) + " sessions" : "—", wht)

    f_cell(dash, 0, 9, "Fades won", dim)
    f_cell(dash, 1, 9, nWin + nLoss > 0 ? str.tostring(math.round(100.0 * nWin / (nWin + nLoss))) + "%  of " + str.tostring(nWin + nLoss) : "—", nWin >= nLoss ? grn : red)


// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ALERTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
if buySignal
    alert("IV Walls FADE LONG | wall " + str.tostring(wallDn, format.mintick) + " | entry " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + " | SL " + str.tostring(buyStop, format.mintick) + " | TP1 " + str.tostring(eT1, format.mintick) + " | TP2 " + str.tostring(eT2, format.mintick) + " | TP3 " + str.tostring(eT3, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if sellSignal
    alert("IV Walls FADE SHORT | wall " + str.tostring(wallUp, format.mintick) + " | entry " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + " | SL " + str.tostring(sellStop, format.mintick) + " | TP1 " + str.tostring(eT1, format.mintick) + " | TP2 " + str.tostring(eT2, format.mintick) + " | TP3 " + str.tostring(eT3, format.mintick), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

alertcondition(buySignal,  "IV Walls — Fade Long",  "IV Walls: fade long at lower wall")
alertcondition(sellSignal, "IV Walls — Fade Short", "IV Walls: fade short at upper wall")
alertcondition(tagUpNow or tagDnNow, "IV Walls — Wall Tagged", "IV Walls: wall tagged")
